    "result": "I implemented `Process` in `inbox.go` and added tests in `inbox_test.go`, but neither has been run. The permission prompt blocked `go vet` and `go test`, so run `go test ./...` yourself.\n\nThe code makes sure a restart after a crash never charges a card twice:\n\n- **Marker before charging:** before `handle` runs, `Process` writes a marker to `dir/processing/\u003cname\u003e`. If `handle` returns an error, the marker is removed and the message is retried on the next run.\n- **Safe result file:** the result goes to a temp file first and is then renamed to `done/\u003cname\u003e`, so a crash never leaves a half-written file.\n- **Crash after charging:** if `done/\u003cname\u003e` exists at startup, the charge already went through. `Process` only removes the message from the inbox and does not call `handle` again.\n- **Crash during charging:** if a marker exists but `done/\u003cname\u003e` does not, nobody knows whether the card was charged. `Process` leaves that message in the inbox and returns an error. It is never retried on its own; a person checks the charge and deletes the marker to allow a retry.\n\nTwo things are still open:\n\n1. **Choice between two risks:** I chose \"may miss a charge, needs a person to check\" over \"may charge twice\". If `handle` can take a key that stops a repeat charge, pass it the message name. Then a stuck message could be retried safely.\n2. **Windows:** directory syncs do nothing on Windows, so a power loss there could still undo a rename or a delete.",
